# Reference Point — Role Card Pattern

When the user says **"reference point"**, **"like the reference point"**, or **"design it like My Role"**, match the `.role-card` component in `#overview`.

For subsection labels (grey eyebrow + title), use the separate **Subsection Head** reference in `reference-point-sub-head.mdc`.

For section intro paragraphs under a display heading, use the **Lead** reference in `reference-point-lead.mdc`.

For gap/problem card labels, use the **Gap Card Label** reference in `reference-point-gap-label.mdc`.

For gap card italic headlines, use the **Gap Card Headline** reference in `reference-point-gap-headline.mdc`.

## Structure

```html
<div class="role-card">
  <p class="eyebrow">Label</p>
  <p class="role-line">Serif italic statement.</p>
  <div class="tags">
    <span class="tag">Tag one</span>
  </div>
</div>
```

Tags are optional; omit the `.tags` block when not needed.

## Visual spec

| Layer | Class | Treatment |
|-------|-------|-----------|
| Container | `.role-card` | `background: var(--bg-role)`, `border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05)`, `border-radius: 16px`, `padding: 1rem 1.25rem`, column flex, `gap: 0.625rem`, `width: 100%` |
| Label | `.role-card .eyebrow` | `0.75rem`, `#6b7280`, weight 500, uppercase via content |
| Body | `.role-line` | `var(--serif)`, italic, `clamp(1.0625rem, 1.6vw, 1.375rem)`, `line-height: 1.35`, `var(--ink)` |
| Tags | `.tag` | pill, `border: 1px solid var(--label)`, `var(--label)`, `0.6875rem`, weight 600, `0.1em` tracking, uppercase |

## Do not

- Reuse brown section `.eyebrow` styling on the card label — card eyebrows are smaller grey (`#6b7280`).
- Swap `.role-line` for sans-serif body text.
- Use `.display` or `.title` inside the card; keep hierarchy flat (eyebrow → role-line → optional tags).
